{
  "dom_id": "step-q152781",
  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }\\frac{5{y}^{2}}{{({y}^{3}-2)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we substitute $u={y}^{3}-2.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}y}=3{y}^{2}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u={y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nSince $u\\to \\infty $ when $y\\to \\infty ,$ the table for the limits of integration using the rule $u={y}^{3}-2$ is as follows:\n\n| $y$ | $3$ | $\\infty $ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $25$ | $\\infty $ |\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable $u$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }\\frac{5{y}^{2}}{{({y}^{3}-2)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{25}^{\\infty }\\frac{5}{{u}^{2}}(\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}{\\int }_{25}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }\\frac{5{y}^{2}}{{({y}^{3}-2)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\frac{5}{3}{\\int }_{25}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}{\\int }_{25}^{\\infty }{u}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{25}^{a}{u}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }[-{u}^{-1}]_{25}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{3}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[\\frac{1}{u}]}_{25}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{3}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\frac{1}{a}-\\frac{1}{25}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{3}(0-\\frac{1}{25}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
